  "answer": "Other users have already requested this feature. It would let you hide chosen windows from screen sharing, recording and screenshots. The usual approach is the WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE display affinity. PowerToys has no such utility today. The main tracking issue is PowerToys#46333 (\"Privacy Overlay\"). It proposes an Always-on-Top-style hotkey that excludes the selected window from capture. A contributor has posted a proof of concept there. PowerToys#48566 was closed as a duplicate of #46333. PowerToys#34950 (\"Window Masking\") asks for the same thing, though it was closed as a duplicate of an unrelated issue. Subscribe to or upvote #46333 to follow progress. Until it ships, share only the specific window or app you intend to show, not the whole screen. Third-party tools such as Invisiwind and winhider can also hide windows from capture."
 },
